body:
This test name implies it verifies client-side routing, but it only checks `#root` HTML length on the initial `/` route and never navigates. Either rename the test to reflect what it asserts, or add an actual route transition (e.g., click a link / `page.goto` to another in-app route) and then assert content to cover routing regressions.
```suggestion
  test('should render the initial route with non-empty root content', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('/');
    await waitForReactMount(page);

    // After the initial route load, the page should have meaningful DOM content
```
